{
  "$doc": [
    "The profiler's records and blocks as the kernel lays them out and the shell reads",
    "them in place (sched/profiler/record.rs, apps/web/src/feature/debug/profiler/view.ts):",
    "word offsets, eight bytes a word, and the names the numbers index. A packed table",
    "gives each field's width and the generator lays the offsets out. Nothing is built",
    "for a read: the kernel writes numbers where they stay, and the words for them are",
    "the shell's."
  ],
  "CENSUS_TAGS": [
    "chunk",
    "decor",
    "ghost_box",
    "ghost_coplanar",
    "ghost_decor",
    "skinned",
    "puck_zone",
    "puck_beacon",
    "badge",
    "debug"
  ],
  "PHASE_NAMES": [
    "interaction",
    "visible",
    "content",
    "cosmetic",
    "report"
  ],
  "CATEGORY_NAMES": [
    "terrain",
    "poi",
    "geocode",
    "geocode_dict",
    "asset",
    "earth"
  ],
  "OUTCOME_NAMES": [
    "ok",
    "aborted",
    "error"
  ],
  "TASK_PHASE_NAMES": [
    "net_ms",
    "bytes",
    "decode_ms",
    "adopt_ms"
  ],
  "STEP_NAMES": [
    "controller",
    "input",
    "camera",
    "environment",
    "companion",
    "preview",
    "sight",
    "goal",
    "demand",
    "chunks",
    "debug_gizmos",
    "profiler"
  ],
  "EFFECT_NAMES": [
    "navigation",
    "bootstrap",
    "geolocation",
    "orientation",
    "follow",
    "destination",
    "view",
    "geocode",
    "decor",
    "chunk_sources",
    "hover",
    "puck",
    "objects",
    "settings",
    "assets",
    "pump"
  ],
  "GPU_SPAN_NAMES": [
    "air",
    "shadow",
    "prepass",
    "ao",
    "world",
    "badges",
    "cases"
  ],
  "LIMITS": {
    "$type": "u32",
    "PHASES_MAX": 6,
    "REASONS": 4,
    "STEP_SLOTS": 32,
    "ZOOMS": 24,
    "$ZOOMS": "A lane a zoom slot, by the zoom itself: slot z holds a cell of zoom z's tiles, past the leaves for the objects' finer cells (pxl-spec space/layer/lattice.rs `Lattice::tile_zoom`)."
  },
  "FRAME": {
    "$type": "u32",
    "$packed": true,
    "$doc": [
      "One rendered frame (sched/profiler/frame.rs FrameSample). `settled` is 0 or 1; `census` pairs draws and triangles in CENSUS_TAGS' order, and `zoom_tris` and `zoom_tiles` hold zoom z in slot z. A lane's name says its unit: `_ms`, `_mb`, and `_zooms` for a set of zooms as bits, bit z for zoom z."
    ],
    "t": 1,
    "dt_ms": 1,
    "frame_ms": 1,
    "settled": 1,
    "sched_ms": 1,
    "budget_ms": 1,
    "phases": "PHASE_NAMES",
    "chunks_ms": 1,
    "task_ms": 1,
    "gpu_ms": 1,
    "gpu_spans": "GPU_SPAN_NAMES",
    "draw_calls": 1,
    "triangles": 1,
    "census": "2 * CENSUS_TAGS",
    "zoom_tris": "LIMITS.ZOOMS",
    "px": 1,
    "gpu_skipped": 1,
    "buffers": 1,
    "buffer_mb": 1,
    "arena_mb": 1,
    "tex_depth_mb": 1,
    "tex_shadow_mb": 1,
    "tex_layers_mb": 1,
    "lod_chunks": 1,
    "lod_in_frustum": 1,
    "lod_pending": 1,
    "lod_settling": 1,
    "lod_offscreen_pending": 1,
    "lod_oldest_release_ms": 1,
    "lod_oldest_visible_ms": 1,
    "mounts_added": 1,
    "mounts_removed": 1,
    "mounts_layouts": 1,
    "tiles_total": 1,
    "zoom_tiles": "LIMITS.ZOOMS",
    "tiles_poi": 1,
    "heap_used_mb": 1,
    "heap_live_mb": 1,
    "heap_run_mb": 1,
    "heap_slot_mb": 1,
    "heap_range_mb": 1,
    "heap_refusals": 1,
    "heap_largest_free_mb": 1,
    "ring_cq_peak": 1,
    "ring_held_peak": 1,
    "work_runs": 1,
    "work_bakes": 1,
    "work_fine_peak": 1,
    "work_coarse_peak": 1,
    "q_terrain": 1,
    "q_poi": 1,
    "stale_hidden": 1,
    "stale_uncovered": 1,
    "stale_unready": 1,
    "slot_waits": 1,
    "slot_wait_zooms": 1,
    "slot_chained": 1,
    "cap_commit_left": 1,
    "cap_mount_left": 1,
    "cap_mount_full": 1,
    "cap_record_refused": 1,
    "turn_effects_ms": 1,
    "turn_stage_ms": 1,
    "turn_step_ms": 1,
    "turn_step_name": 1,
    "cover_rule": 1,
    "cover_drawn": 1,
    "cover_gaps": 1,
    "view_rays": 1,
    "view_visits": 1
  },
  "FRAME_GROUPS": {
    "$doc": [
      "What each of the report's lines prints of a frame, FRAME's lanes in groups: a lane's label is its name without the group's prefix, and every lane is in one group (lane.test.ts), so a lane the kernel adds is printed without a word written for it. The order is what a reader asks in turn — where the time went, what was drawn, what the chunk scheduler is doing, what it built and fetched, and what it all holds — and the report and the panel both follow it."
    ],
    "pace": [
      "t",
      "dt_ms",
      "frame_ms",
      "settled",
      "sched_ms",
      "budget_ms",
      "phases",
      "chunks_ms",
      "task_ms"
    ],
    "turn": [
      "turn_effects_ms",
      "turn_stage_ms",
      "turn_step_ms",
      "turn_step_name"
    ],
    "gpu": [
      "gpu_ms",
      "gpu_spans",
      "draw_calls",
      "triangles",
      "census",
      "zoom_tris",
      "px",
      "gpu_skipped"
    ],
    "lod": [
      "lod_chunks",
      "lod_in_frustum",
      "lod_pending",
      "lod_settling",
      "lod_offscreen_pending",
      "lod_oldest_release_ms",
      "lod_oldest_visible_ms"
    ],
    "mounts": [
      "mounts_added",
      "mounts_removed",
      "mounts_layouts"
    ],
    "stale": [
      "stale_hidden",
      "stale_uncovered",
      "stale_unready"
    ],
    "slot": [
      "slot_waits",
      "slot_wait_zooms",
      "slot_chained"
    ],
    "cap": [
      "cap_commit_left",
      "cap_mount_left",
      "cap_mount_full",
      "cap_record_refused"
    ],
    "work": [
      "work_runs",
      "work_bakes",
      "work_fine_peak",
      "work_coarse_peak"
    ],
    "q": [
      "q_terrain",
      "q_poi"
    ],
    "tiles": [
      "tiles_total",
      "zoom_tiles",
      "tiles_poi"
    ],
    "cover": [
      "cover_rule",
      "cover_drawn",
      "cover_gaps"
    ],
    "view": [
      "view_rays",
      "view_visits"
    ],
    "device": [
      "buffers",
      "buffer_mb",
      "arena_mb",
      "tex_depth_mb",
      "tex_shadow_mb",
      "tex_layers_mb"
    ],
    "heap": [
      "heap_used_mb",
      "heap_live_mb",
      "heap_run_mb",
      "heap_slot_mb",
      "heap_range_mb",
      "heap_refusals",
      "heap_largest_free_mb"
    ],
    "ring": [
      "ring_cq_peak",
      "ring_held_peak"
    ]
  },
  "TASK": {
    "$type": "u32",
    "$packed": true,
    "$doc": [
      "One settled task (sched/profiler/task.rs TaskRow). `subject` is a u64 word and every other word an f64; `start_ms` is NaN for a task that never ran; `category`, `outcome` and each of `phase_ids` index CATEGORY_NAMES, OUTCOME_NAMES and TASK_PHASE_NAMES. `at_file` is the address of the file name, `at_file_bytes` long, of the line a failure was made at, and 0 where the failure was the host's."
    ],
    "category": 1,
    "subject": 1,
    "priority": 1,
    "enqueue_ms": 1,
    "start_ms": 1,
    "end_ms": 1,
    "outcome": 1,
    "fail": 1,
    "detail": 1,
    "at_file": 1,
    "at_file_bytes": 1,
    "at_line": 1,
    "phase_count": 1,
    "phase_ids": "LIMITS.PHASES_MAX",
    "phase_values": "LIMITS.PHASES_MAX"
  },
  "WORST": {
    "$type": "u32",
    "$packed": true,
    "$doc": [
      "One of the window's worst frames and the frame before it, which is zero where `has_prev` is 0."
    ],
    "sample": "FRAME",
    "has_prev": 1,
    "prev": "FRAME"
  },
  "SPREAD": {
    "$type": "u32",
    "$packed": true,
    "p50": 1,
    "p95": 1,
    "max": 1
  },
  "TASK_SUMMARY": {
    "$type": "u32",
    "$packed": true,
    "$doc": [
      "One category's tasks in the window, at SUMMARY.tasks + its index × WORDS. Each reason is (fail, detail, n), commonest first; `phase_mean` is NaN for a phase no task reported. `tick_per_bake` elsewhere is NaN where there were no bakes."
    ],
    "n": 1,
    "ok": 1,
    "aborted": 1,
    "error": 1,
    "lat": "SPREAD",
    "reason_count": 1,
    "reasons": "3 * LIMITS.REASONS",
    "phase_n": 1,
    "phase_mean": "TASK_PHASE_NAMES"
  },
  "STEP": {
    "$type": "u32",
    "$packed": true,
    "$doc": [
      "One registered step's timing, at SUMMARY.steps.slots + its index × WORDS. `name` indexes STEP_NAMES."
    ],
    "phase": 1,
    "name": 1,
    "ms": 1,
    "count": 1,
    "max_ms": 1
  },
  "SUMMARY": {
    "$type": "u32",
    "$packed": true,
    "$doc": [
      "The block PROFILER_READ computes: each section's words at its AT, the fields relative to it. Every word an f64. Packed: a section's AT is where the one before it ends, and the block's WORDS where the last ends, both laid out by the generator."
    ],
    "rec": {
      "recording": 1,
      "elapsed_ms": 1,
      "tasks": 1,
      "frames": 1,
      "truncated": 1
    },
    "frames": {
      "present": 1,
      "n": 1,
      "seconds": 1,
      "moving": 1,
      "missed": 1,
      "overran": 1,
      "dt": "SPREAD",
      "task": "SPREAD",
      "offthread": "SPREAD",
      "gpu": "SPREAD",
      "sched": "SPREAD",
      "chunks": "SPREAD",
      "phases": "PHASE_NAMES * SPREAD",
      "gpu_spans": "GPU_SPAN_NAMES * SPREAD",
      "per_s_runs": 1,
      "per_s_bakes": 1,
      "backlog_s": 1,
      "backlog_per_s_runs": 1,
      "backlog_per_s_bakes": 1,
      "chunks_per_bake": 1,
      "mounts_added": 1,
      "mounts_removed": 1,
      "used_delta_mb": 1,
      "census": "2 * CENSUS_TAGS",
      "zoom_tris": "LIMITS.ZOOMS",
      "last": "FRAME"
    },
    "tasks": {
      "slots": "CATEGORY_NAMES * TASK_SUMMARY"
    },
    "counters": {
      "faces_kept": 1,
      "faces_possible": 1,
      "runs_culled": 1,
      "runs_total": 1,
      "coarse_boxes": 1,
      "coarse_low_fill": 1,
      "built_runs": 1,
      "built_bakes": 1,
      "built_starved": 1,
      "atlas_repacks": 1,
      "atlas_uploads": 1
    },
    "atlas": {
      "size": 1,
      "entries": 1,
      "shelves": 1,
      "used_px": 1,
      "initial": 1
    },
    "held": {
      "run_sets": 1,
      "run_set_mb": 1,
      "tiers": 1,
      "decor_blocks": 1,
      "decor_instances": 1,
      "decor_bytes": 1
    },
    "fetch": {
      "queued": 1,
      "running": 1,
      "credits": 1
    },
    "peak": {
      "present": 1,
      "dt_ms": 1,
      "sched_ms": 1,
      "chunks_ms": 1,
      "gpu_ms": 1,
      "draw_calls": 1,
      "triangles": 1,
      "q_terrain": 1,
      "q_poi": 1,
      "chunks": 1,
      "in_frustum": 1,
      "pending": 1,
      "settling": 1,
      "offscreen_pending": 1,
      "oldest_release_ms": 1,
      "oldest_visible_ms": 1,
      "fine_peak": 1,
      "coarse_peak": 1
    },
    "steps": {
      "count": 1,
      "slots": "LIMITS.STEP_SLOTS * STEP"
    },
    "quality": {
      "step": 1,
      "star": 1,
      "frames_held": 1,
      "admitted": 1,
      "evicted": 1,
      "refined": 1,
      "changes_peak": 1
    },
    "heap": {
      "$doc": [
        "The heap as the read finds it, recording or not: `used_mb` its top, `requests` the pages it has ever asked for."
      ],
      "used_mb": 1,
      "requests": 1
    },
    "view": {
      "$doc": [
        "Where the camera and the pointer are as the read finds them, recording or not: angles in radians, `dist` and `hover_x`..`hover_z` in units, `center_z` and `hover_alt` in metres, and NaN where there is none. `chunk_zoom` is the zoom of the drawn chunk's cells under the pointer, `tier_zoom` the zoom its tier is drawn at and `read_zoom` that of the tile it is read from."
      ],
      "dist": 1,
      "polar": 1,
      "azimuth": 1,
      "tau": 1,
      "center_lon": 1,
      "center_lat": 1,
      "center_z": 1,
      "hover_x": 1,
      "hover_y": 1,
      "hover_z": 1,
      "hover_lon": 1,
      "hover_lat": 1,
      "hover_alt": 1,
      "chunk_zoom": 1,
      "tier_zoom": 1,
      "read_zoom": 1
    }
  },
  "READ": {
    "$type": "u32",
    "$packed": true,
    "$doc": [
      "What PROFILER_READ answers with the address of: u32 words, each range's address in the module's memory and its record count."
    ],
    "summary_at": 1,
    "summary_words": 1,
    "frames_at": 1,
    "frames_count": 1,
    "tasks_at": 1,
    "tasks_count": 1,
    "worst_at": 1,
    "worst_count": 1
  },
  "LOG": {
    "$type": "u32",
    "$packed": true,
    "$doc": [
      "What PROFILER_TAKE answers with the address of: u32 words, the frames and tasks the stream has kept since the last take."
    ],
    "frames_at": 1,
    "frames_count": 1,
    "tasks_at": 1,
    "tasks_count": 1
  }
}
